@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:build] editor-official-source
The editor MUST compile the reviewed Microsoft Code OSS source commit with the
maintained patch stack. Microsoft product binaries, downstream editor runtimes,
Microsoft Marketplace product add-ons and unpinned dependencies MUST NOT enter
the shipped output. Only the declared signed, hash-pinned Open VSX defaults may
be added as third-party builtin extensions.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:build;security] editor-bundled-extension-inputs
The builtin defaults MUST be exactly elixir-lsp.elixir-ls,
EditorConfig.EditorConfig, rust-lang.rust-analyzer and cab404.vscode-direnv at
stable, engine-compatible universal versions in extensions.lock.json. Whole
VSIX signatures MUST be verified by the packaged verifier/key ring before
publication; hashes, archive paths, identities, platform and undeclared
dependencies/packs MUST also be checked. Payload bytes and notices MUST remain
unchanged, and shared extension code MUST remain immutable.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:product] editor-builtin-personal-control
Builtin defaults MUST preserve upstream personal disable and newer-version
override behavior. They MUST NOT create a shared writable extension/data
directory or repeatedly seed a personal installation. Upstream builtin
extensions are not uninstallable; independently installed extensions remain
under the user's install, disable and uninstall controls.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:build] editor-project-language-tools
The shipped language defaults MUST delegate to project PATH tools without
running bundled language bootstrap installers or adding global language
toolchain/server packages. Missing Elixir adapter commands MUST refuse with fixed
stderr and exit 127. Elixir adapters MUST preserve all caller arguments.
The Rust default MUST resolve rust-analyzer directly from project PATH;
an absent executable retains the native ENOENT refusal.
User-supplied server overrides remain project choices under existing egress.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:product] editor-bundled-ai-disabled
Bundled Copilot and core AI/chat MUST remain disabled after conflicting settings,
restored state and direct command invocation. Generic completion and independently
installed extensions MUST retain their independent user controls.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:product;security] editor-all-folder-trust
Editor workers MUST disable workspace trust for all guest folders; settings MUST
NOT restore Restricted Mode. This choice MUST NOT automatically allow .envrc or
change Marshall authorization, personal identity or guest isolation boundaries.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:build;security] editor-extension-pin-maintenance
Maintenance MUST update only the four declared extension pins, selecting
explicit stable compatible metadata across bounded consistent pages. It MUST
reuse packaged signature/engine validation and MUST NOT trust registry keys,
expand dependency scope, execute language bootstrap, install on the host,
update the editor baseline or commit/deploy. Complete validation precedes atomic
lock replacement and file/parent synchronization; failures before replacement
and observed concurrent lock edits MUST preserve the existing lock. A parent
synchronization failure after replacement MUST report durability_unknown with
publication_durability_unknown; the complete new lock may already be visible.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] editor-gallery-signatures
User Open VSX gallery installation, including browser extensions and dependencies,
MUST verify the entire VSIX against reviewed packaged Ed25519 keys before extraction.
Missing, malformed, oversized or untrusted signatures MUST fail regardless of user
signature settings. Explicit local VSIX imports remain a separate unverified path.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] editor-isolated-assets
The served workbench MUST use the broker-provided HTTPS editor origin and separate
HTTPS hash webview origins. Missing or invalid trusted configuration MUST fail;
Microsoft CDN URLs MUST NOT be used as asset fallbacks.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:build] editor-release-identity
The editor and webview assets MUST be published from the same source build. The
release descriptor MUST identify the source commit, protocol version and all
maintained patches, trusted keys, product settings and pinned dependency inputs,
including the extension lock and maintained validation/extraction/adapters.
